  "ref_idx": 0,
  "model": "claude-sonnet-5",
  "code": "import backtrader as bt\n\n\nclass CandleBodyVolumeBreakoutStrategy(bt.Strategy):\n    params = (\n        ('body_period', 20),\n        ('volume_period', 20),\n        ('body_mult', 1.5),\n        ('volume_mult', 1.5),\n        ('enable_short', True),\n        ('session_start_hour', 7),\n        ('session_start_minute', 0),\n        ('session_end_hour', 17),\n        ('session_end_minute', 0),\n    )\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.body = abs(self.data.close - self.data.open)\n        self.sma_body = bt.indicators.SMA(self.body, period=self.p.body_period)\n        self.sma_volume = bt.indicators.SMA(self.data.volume, period=self.p.volume_period)\n        self.order = None\n\n    def notify_order(self, order):\n        if order.status in (order.Completed, order.Canceled, order.Margin, order.Rejected):\n            self.order = None\n\n    def next(self):\n        if self.order:\n            return\n\n        close = self.data.close[0]\n        open_ = self.data.open[0]\n        volume = self.data.volume[0]\n        body = self.body[0]\n        sma_body = self.sma_body[0]\n        sma_volume = self.sma_volume[0]\n\n        long_signal = (close > open_) and (body >= self.p.body_mult * sma_body) and (volume >= self.p.volume_mult * sma_volume)\n        short_signal = (close < open_) and (body >= self.p.body_mult * sma_body) and (volume >= self.p.volume_mult * sma_volume)\n\n        t = self.data.datetime.time(0)\n        start = (self.p.session_start_hour, self.p.session_start_minute)\n        end = (self.p.session_end_hour, self.p.session_end_minute)\n        time_ok = start <= (t.hour, t.minute) <= end\n\n        if self.position:\n            if self.position.size > 0 and short_signal:\n                self.order = self.close()\n            elif self.position.size < 0 and long_signal:\n                self.order = self.close()\n        else:\n            if time_ok and long_signal:\n                self.order = self.buy()\n            elif self.p.enable_short and time_ok and short_signal:\n                self.order = self.sell()",
  "assumptions": [
    {
      "topic": "infeasible",
      "choice": "Signals computed directly on the harness-provided 1h AAPL bars rather than 2h/4h bars.",
      "reason": "The spec calls for 2-hour or 4-hour bars, but the execution environment fixes a single 1h PandasData feed added by the harness; resampling to a different timeframe is a cerebro-level data-feed configuration (cerebro.resampledata) that cannot be performed from inside a bt.Strategy subclass, and only one data feed is available. The closest literal reading is to apply the stated body/volume/time logic to the bars actually supplied."
    },
    {
      "topic": "short entry toggle",
      "choice": "Implemented shorting as a strategy parameter enable_short defaulted to True.",
      "reason": "The spec labels the short entry 'if enabled' but also fully specifies its condition and a corresponding exit rule for closing shorts on a long signal, indicating shorting is part of the intended behavior with an on/off switch; True was chosen as the default so the full spec (both entry types and both exit legs) is active out of the box."
    },
    {
      "topic": "time window scope",
      "choice": "The 07:00-17:00 time filter gates only new entries (buy/sell to open); exit/close signals are evaluated on every bar regardless of time.",
      "reason": "The spec states 'Trades may only be opened when...' tying the window specifically to opening trades, while the exit rule is stated separately with no time qualifier."
    },
    {
      "topic": "no open position",
      "choice": "Interpreted as fully flat (self.position size == 0); entries require no existing position of either direction.",
      "reason": "Both long and short entry conditions state 'AND no open position' with no distinction by direction, consistent with the canonical default of holding at most one position at a time."
    }
